+rendering invalidation, visual selection, yanking, and polling background workers. Insert mode sends
+chat text to the selected agent session, or to `command-agent` when the Work Leaf command surface is
+selected. Bracketed-paste newlines and Shift+Enter are chat prompt line breaks. A plain Enter submits
+the buffered chat text. Command mode supports vim-style visual selection in either pane: `v` selects
+characters, `V` selects rendered lines, Ctrl-V selects rectangular blocks, and `h/j/k/l` or arrow
+keys move the visual cursor. `y` yanks the selected text, and `Y` yanks complete lines. Yanked text
+is emitted through an OSC52 terminal clipboard sequence and a transient status notice reports the
+character count. Visual selection is terminal-local state and is cleared by Escape, pane changes,
+mouse actions, and scrolling. When an agent chat is selected in command mode, `/` focuses the chat,
+seeds the chat buffer with `/`, and enters insert mode so `/status`-style input submits through the
+same selected-agent chat path.
 
